{:org/id :org-jpn-minsei-iin
 :org/form-family :family-lay-public-office
 :org/name "民生委員・児童委員 (Japanese welfare commissioners)"
 :org/entity-kind :org-form
 :org/category :cat-local-place
 :org/type :secular-community
 :org/scope :national
 :org/region-primary :region-asia-east
 :org/countries ["JP"]
 :org/founding-date 1917
 :org/founding-note "Descends from the 済世顧問制度 (1917) and 方面委員制度 — a century-old lay welfare office."
 :org/member-count 226000
 :org/member-count-basis "source-pinned: an authorized establishment of about 241,000 posts, of which roughly 15,000 were VACANT at the December 2022 nationwide reappointment — a fill rate of 93.7%. The next three-year cycle began December 2025. Recruitment shortfall is now the sector's headline problem, driven by both rising establishment and falling willingness to serve (全国民生委員児童委員連合会)."
 :org/legal-registration :statutory-no-personality
 :org/registration-note "Commissioners are unpaid special local public servants appointed by the Minister of Health, Labour and Welfare — statutory office, no salary, no legal entity of their own."
 :org/governance-model :hierarchical
 :org/mission-statement "Neighborhood-assigned lay commissioners who visit isolated older people, connect households to welfare services and act as the eyes of the safety net — Japan's frontline welfare capacity is a volunteer roster with a 6% hole in it."
 :org/related-org "org-jpn-chonaikai"
 :org/source-name "全国民生委員児童委員連合会「令和4年12月の民生委員・児童委員一斉改選結果に関する総括となりて確保のための提案」"
 :org/source-url "https://www.yokohamashakyo.jp/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/r412_teian.pdf"
 :org/source-date "2022-12"
 :org/source-tier :primary
 :org/pinned-on "2026-07-26"
 :org/data-provenance "source-pinned"
 :source/dataset "community-coverage"}

